      "content": "that sounds like a good start. but i feel like i need to address the elephant in the room. some of the older board members are really pushing back, saying that anything other than maximizing shareholder value is basically a breach of fiduciary duty and just \"virtue signaling.\" can u help me write a section that basically shuts down those arguments? like, how do i frame it so it's clear that the old way of just chasing quarterly profits is actually outdated and risky compared to this new ESG approach?",
